Subject: [PATCH 406/407] SableOS: Sable accent on the Theme step, Theme after
 Privacy

The Theme step keeps LineageOS's Dark/Light choice, which writes
UiModeManager, the system theme Quick Settings uses and Sable apps
follow. Under it the step now shows the Sable accent stored in the
org.sableos.appearance authority (Settings patch 0101) and a Change
accent button that opens Settings > Display scrolled to the Accent row.

Setup does not write the accent: the authority only accepts writes from
Settings, Sable Start and App display compatibility, so writing it here
would need a new writer or a second store. Settings stores the accent
and seeds the system palette, and the step re-reads it when the user
returns. When the authority is absent or unreadable the accent rows stay
hidden and the step is LineageOS's own.

In the owner script the Theme step moves from after screen lock to right
after Privacy, the order the Sable setup design gives (privacy, then
theme, then date and time). The secondary-user script is unchanged.

The accent values and Settings extras are in the pure SableAccent class.

